    A group of rows: contiguous rows on a container with large corners, which is
    what the phone's own settings have looked like for several versions and what
    androidx.preference has no idea about.

    Measured off a Pixel 8's Settings at 365 dpi rather than taken from a
    document, since there is no published one: the radii by fitting a circle to
    the corner's alpha profile, the rest by finding the edges of the container in
    a screenshot. What came back was 15.8 dp and 14.9 dp for the two ends of a
    group, 3.95 dp between rows, 2.19 dp of gap, 20.6 dp between groups and
    15.78 dp either side.
-->
<resources>

    <dimen name="group_radius">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_radius_inner">4dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_inset">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_gap">2dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_spacing">20dp</dimen>
    <!-- Either side of a row that is its own container: a text field's box does
         not want a card behind it, and 2 dp from one reads as a mistake. -->
    <dimen name="group_gap_field">8dp</dimen>

    <!-- Around a card on the home screen, which with the list's own padding
         either side comes to the same 16 dp a group of rows is inset by. -->
    <dimen name="card_margin">8dp</dimen>

    <!--
        A screen's header, which is a heading over the groups under it and is
        inset like one: 24 dp, where a container's own edge is 16. Flush with
        the container reads as unaligned, because a 16 dp corner means the
        content inside it starts further in than the edge does.

        A button in a header is the phone's own: a 40 dp filled circle in the
        middle of the 48 dp that can be hit. Which is why what a header is told
        about its buttons is 4 dp less — the circle carries the alignment, and
        the touch target is larger than it.
    -->
    <dimen name="header_inset">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="header_inset_button">20dp</dimen>

    <!-- Above and below it. A header is a bar's height wherever it appears —
         on a screen, where it is one, and over a sheet, where it is not — so
         this is what is left either side of the 48 dp a button takes. -->
    <dimen name="header_padding">4dp</dimen>

    <!-- Inside a row, and inside a heading over a group of them. -->
    <dimen name="row_padding">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="row_min_height">56dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_inset">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_padding_top">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_padding_bottom">12dp</dimen>

</resources>
